WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.859
The MCU has provided us with a whole lot of
unique smooches -- but which sweep fans off

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:08.550
their feet and which fall flat?

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:12.519
From Tony and Pepper to Peggy and Steve, we're
ranking them all.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:18.610
Nat and Bruce's uncomfortable coupling pops
up from the depths of nowhere during Avengers:

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:24.060
Age of Ultron, built out of forced conversations
and a lust that just isn't believable.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.770
Though some fans believed the franchise to
be building up Natasha and Clint as a potential

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.360
item, Age of Ultron reveals that Hawkeye actually
has a hidden family.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.340
Apparently, writer/director Joss Whedon felt
he had to give Nat a love interest.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.340
And he chose...

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.340
Bruce.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.699
While the couple are hunkered down at the
Barton family compound, Natasha reveals her

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:46.429
forced sterilization to Bruce.

00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:51.159
Here, Black Widow stumbles into tired tropes
by calling herself a monster for what her

00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:52.379
captors did.

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:53.379
The kicker?

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:58.069
Though clearly horrified, Bruce doesn't try
to comfort her or, even just tell her she's

00:00:58.069 --> 00:01:01.219
not a monster because she can't have kids.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:05.290
That's not exactly the message a superhero
franchise should be sending.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:10.080
A while after that cringeworthy exchange,
they kiss, right before she throws him off

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.150
a cliff to enlist the help of "the other guy"
known as Hulk.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:19.530
There's nothing cuter than throwing your oblivious
lover off a cliff so he can save the day!

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:23.650
When exactly did Black Widow become a damsel,
and who greenlit this arc?

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:29.240
Outside of exchanging an uncomfortable look
in Avengers: Infinity War, we never hear from

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.841
the doomed pairing ever again.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:37.370
Seriously, Steve — it's pretty awkward when
the girl you really want to kiss is dead,

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:40.760
but you shouldn't go after her grand-niece
instead.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:45.350
We know Steve Rogers misses Peggy Carter in
Captain America: Civil War.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:49.560
But the solution to that problem is to get
a grief counselor, not make out with your

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.159
dead girlfriend's distant relative.

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:56.900
Who wants to put some cash on whether or not
Steve comes clean to Peggy about the incident

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:00.510
when he goes back to the past in Avengers:
Endgame?

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.590
Smart money's on no.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.460
After Sharon Carter and Steve get hot and
heavy on a deserted bridge underpass, Bucky

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.319
and Sam give Cap the Respect Nod.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:12.709
It doesn't make anything less weird, though.

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:15.430
In fact, it might make it creepier.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:20.909
To make matters worse, Steve's time travel
in Endgame might make Sharon his own great-niece

00:02:20.909 --> 00:02:23.040
by marriage in an alternate timeline.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.319
Do Marvel fans really need a long-winded romantic
flashback between Meredith Quill and the guy

00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:32.599
who covertly gives her a tumor years later?

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:35.040
Maybe not, but we get it anyway.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.900
Following a romantic ride in Ego's car, the
happy couple have a rendezvous in the forest

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:45.129
where Ego makes a sinister speech about his
weird plant taking over the world... before

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:47.150
he lays one on Meredith.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.620
She's too smitten to notice how shady her
spaceman is being.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.180
His name is Ego, after all.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:57.870
Fans may not know the extent of Ego's misdeeds
at the beginning of Guardians of the Galaxy

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.220
Volume 2, when the flashback takes place.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:06.779
However, Ego's villainous plot twist later
completely sours the scene, making it difficult

00:03:06.779 --> 00:03:08.689
to watch after the initial viewing.

00:03:08.689 --> 00:03:13.799
But hey, at least he and Meredith make out
to the sweet sounds of Looking Glass's "Brandy"

00:03:13.799 --> 00:03:15.150
before he kills her?

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.829
They'll always have that.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.379
Thanks for ruining a classic, Ego.

00:03:19.939 --> 00:03:24.120
There's nothing really terrible to be said
about Thor and Jane Foster, other than the

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.639
fact that they have little to no chemistry.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:31.209
Both are great characters in their own right,
but nothing makes them work as a pair.

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:35.409
When they kiss in Thor, it looks like they're
trying to eat each other's faces, and it's

00:03:35.409 --> 00:03:37.010
just hard to watch.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:41.950
He might be the God of Thunder, but he doesn't
exactly make Jane quake during the scene.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:46.520
Thor promises to come back for her when he
leaves for Asgard, but we'd honestly rather

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:47.730
he didn't.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:52.029
He came, he saw, he kind of conquered — now
it's time to move on.

00:03:52.029 --> 00:03:55.040
"Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you."

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.510
"She didn't dump me.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:57.510
I dumped her.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.890
It was a mutual dumping!"

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:04.019
Beyond that uncomfortable kiss, their relationship
never really goes anywhere.

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:07.420
The kiss is all build-up for no payout.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:12.159
Beyond some basic attraction, the pairing
is a subplot at best, and both characters

00:04:12.159 --> 00:04:13.430
deserve better.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:18.340
For fans who did enjoy their pairing, there's
never much closure to their relationship beyond

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:23.790
an off-screen breakup, making the whole affair
that much more disappointing and insignificant.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:30.630
The MCU certainly prioritizes action over
relationship building, but fans won't invest

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:36.130
in a pairing if the entire build-up happens
off-screen without so much as a conversation.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:41.250
As a result, it's almost jarring when Vision
and Wanda kiss in Infinity War.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.900
The last time we saw the couple, they were
feuding in Civil War.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:49.000
But now, fans are supposed to buy that the
pair are blissfully in love when they share

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.500
a tender kiss in a hotel room?

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:56.070
With a little more work, this kiss could have
been one of the best kisses in the MCU.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:05:01.840
But without explaining how Wanda and Vision
got together, it just feels out of place.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:06.830
The movie desperately needs to give some context
to their relationship before zeroing in on

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.390
it — especially for fans who aren't familiar
with their history in the comics.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:17.390
Heck, even fans who devoured their on-page
love story could use a scene or two to acclimate

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:18.390
them!

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:23.570
While the MCU may be known for throwing couples
together without much groundwork, Scott and

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:28.350
Hope arguably have one of the best-built relationships
in the franchise.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:33.530
Both Ant-Man films have significant emotional
build-up between Scott and Hope, with their

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.720
dynamic unraveling at a reasonable pace.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:42.240
In Ant-Man and the Wasp, Marvel turns the
tide on the usual damsel in distress angle:

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:46.350
Wasp saves Ant-Man from drowning, instead
of the other way around.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:51.940
It's also lovely to see Wasp taking the initiative,
leading the relief-driven kiss once she knows

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:53.280
he'll be okay.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.750
It certainly doesn't hurt that both characters
share namespace in the movie title, making

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.810
them equal partners in every sense of the
word.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:06.520
One member of most MCU pairs usually takes
a backseat to the other — and it's usually

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:07.520
the woman.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.830
In a refreshing change of pace, Hope wears
the pants in her relationship with Scott,

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.720
and fans can't get enough of their healthy
bond.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:20.590
Given that most MCU characters are full-on
adults, there's not usually a place in the

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:25.560
franchise for high school romance — until
Marvel finally got to add Spider-Man into

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:26.560
the mix.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:31.930
Tom Holland brings MCU fans arguably the best
live-action rendition of Spider-Man we've

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:37.450
ever seen, and his chemistry with Zendaya
as MJ is off the charts.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:43.680
The pair's first kiss is as adorkably awkward
as one might expect, and it only makes them

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.170
more endearing.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:49.330
After a whole lot of build-up in Spider-Man:
Homecoming, the young couple finally stops

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:52.890
trying to fight their feelings in Spider-Man:
Far From Home.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:57.810
There's nothing quite like a genocidal maniac
wiping out half the population to put things

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.110
into perspective, right?

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:05.210
Following Spider-Man's defeat of Mysterio,
MJ and an unmasked Peter Parker share a few

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:09.640
tentative kisses before getting their bearings
and really going for it.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:14.490
MJ and Spider-Man are both misfits, which
makes them perfect for each other: He's a

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:19.420
nerdy high schooler who saves the world sometimes,
and she's a brilliant young woman who just

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:22.800
can't keep from telling the brutally honest
truth.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:24.250
"I'm not Spider-Man."

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.870
"I mean, I've been watching you for like a
while now.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:29.960
It's kind of obvious."

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:33.360
It's a match made in the library — and on
the battlefield.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:40.390
Unlike most MCU kisses, T'Challa and Nakia
don't lock lips in a blaze of glory during

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:43.900
a massive fight sequence -– and it makes
all the difference.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:48.510
Instead, the couple has a quiet moment to
themselves in Black Panther, where they confess

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.060
their feelings.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:54.740
Entirely secure with himself, T'Challa doesn't
get weird about being saved by a woman.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.420
He thanks Nakia for rescuing him and asks
her to stay.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:04.660
Then, of course, they share a sweet and passionate
kiss away from prying eyes and the usual explosions

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.950
that accompany Marvel romance.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:12.040
Sure, high-action romance scenes are fun,
but this feels much more real and authentic

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:15.040
than most of the MCU's defining kisses.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:19.050
It's nice to see the franchise go for some
realistic build-up instead of throwing in

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:22.360
a few moments of flirtation between world-saving.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:27.389
It's rare for fans to feel like they can see
themselves in an MCU relationship, but during

00:08:27.389 --> 00:08:33.010
this moment, you forget about super suits
and superpowers: The characters just are.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.010
We need more of this energy, Marvel!

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:40.460
Tony and Pepper's coupling is tumultuous,
but nothing less would have done the couple

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:41.460
justice.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:47.210
Given that Robert Downey Jr.'s Iron Man kicked
off the MCU back in 2008 with a self-titled

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.930
movie, he needed a fierce woman to stand by
his side.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:56.110
Enter Gwyneth Paltrow's Pepper Potts, who
gives the playboy superhero a run for his

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:57.110
money.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:09:02.440
It takes two films filled with sass, a moderate
amount of disdain, and a rocky back-and-forth

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:07.650
relationship before the couple shares their
best on-screen kiss in Iron Man 2.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:12.680
On a rooftop overlooking the burning city,
Pepper and Tony can't stop themselves from

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.880
a hardcore make-out session.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.520
It's no matter, apparently, that Pepper said
she was quitting five seconds before they

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:23.370
locked lips, or that they are in the middle
of an argument.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:26.190
It's all very Marvel, and very Tony and Pepper.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:34.070
Unlike most Snap disappearances, Clint's loved
ones are lost to Thanos' brutality in a full-fledged

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.010
scene full of darkness.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:40.530
Since Clint is one of the only Avengers to
have a family we've followed for years, this

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:42.260
loss hits hard.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.590
But what's even worse?

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:48.810
We have to watch Clint mourn them for the
entirety of Endgame, listening to old voicemails

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.230
and falling apart at every turn.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:55.900
The guy just can't catch a break, and it's
pretty traumatic for everyone.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.430
After mourning alongside him for the whole
film and watching Iron Man go out in a blaze

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:05.680
of glory, Clint's reunion with his family
in that cursed field is one of the Endgame's

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.750
most cathartic moments.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:11.890
Following a tear-filled moment with his kids,
Clint gets to kiss his wife for the first

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.440
time in five years.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:18.580
The embrace is short and sweet, but it's one
of the most significant kisses in the MCU

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:22.820
— and it makes his best friend Natasha's
earlier sacrifice that much more meaningful.

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:29.380
In a milestone moment for one of the best
romances in the MCU, Peggy kisses Steve right

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:33.360
before defeating a Nazi in Captain America:
The First Avenger.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.360
And really, isn't that the American dream?

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:40.630
There's just enough build-up between Peggy
and Steve for their heated kiss to make a

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:45.290
long-lasting impact on Cap and the entire
MCU fandom.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:49.860
No one, including Steve, ever really gets
over this whirlwind romance.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:54.770
Peggy and Steve's epic love ripples through
the whole franchise, all the way up to Cap's

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:59.360
final journey through time in Endgame, back
into Peggy's arms.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:04.510
Their fireworks-filled kiss is one of the
most impactful in the entire franchise.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:09.980
How many other people can say that they pined
for a woman for over 70 years after just one

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:10.980
smooch?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:16.940
The best kiss in the MCU is a kiss on the
forehead from a father to his daughter.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:21.980
After so much tragedy, watching Tony Stark
be a good dad is one of the greatest joys

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.610
of Avengers: Endgame.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:29.040
He may not get to enjoy domesticity for very
long, but in those years, Tony gets to be

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.740
a loving husband and father in the middle
of nowhere.

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:37.630
It's incredible to watch him go from rich
playboy to world-saving hero to loving family

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.630
man.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:43.630
Iron Man made the MCU possible in 2008, and
his relationship with his daughter Morgan

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:48.150
marks the beginning of the MCU's heart-wrenching
goodbye to his character.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:53.050
After he tells her a terrible bedtime story,
Tony kisses his daughter on the forehead and

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:54.460
tells her he loves her.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:55.460
Her response:

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.390
"I love you 3,000."

00:11:57.390 --> 00:12:03.830
Turns out to be one of the most poignant quotes
not just in Endgame, but in all of the MCU.

